-- The admin gets three roles, a first name per account and a choice for the mail about Wikipedia (#1156): `owner`, `editor` and `author` take the place of `beheerder` and `moderator`, and every account that was there becomes `editor`. The owner's own account becomes `owner` with `admin create <address> owner` on the host, never here: no address goes in the repository.
-- The list of roles first gets all five values, so the accounts can move over, and then loses the two old ones. The log gets the four actions of the accounts at the end of its list, so no row of it changes.
-- The statements can run again: MariaDB cannot undo DDL, so a migration that stopped halfway finishes on the next start.
-- To undo it on the host: remove the rows with an `account.` action from `audit_log` and put its list back without them; drop `conflict_mail` and `first_name`; give `role` the five values, set every account to `beheerder`, and give it `enum('beheerder','moderator')` again.
ALTER TABLE `admin_users` MODIFY COLUMN `role` enum('beheerder','moderator','owner','editor','author') NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `admin_users` SET `role` = 'editor' WHERE `role` IN ('beheerder', 'moderator');--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE `admin_users` MODIFY COLUMN `role` enum('owner','editor','author') NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
